2.25.1

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
free_transition_pgtable();
machine_kexec_free_page_tables(image);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because both `free_transition_pgtable()` and `machine_kexec_free_page_tables(image)` are called when memory allocation fails during the kexec loading process. This results in double freeing of the same memory, leading to crashes.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
image->arch.pgd = NULL;
image->arch.pmd0 = NULL;
image->arch.pte0 = NULL;
```
Reason:
The patch fixes the bug by setting the pointers to `NULL` after freeing the memory. This prevents subsequent calls to free the same memory again, ensuring that double free attempts do not occur, thus avoiding crashes.

